Description: CVE-2026-109619 - Avoid state corruption via stale request state in session upload progress
 Persistent PHP workers (mod_php/FPM) could keep global error, session,
 object or extension state pointing into freed request memory after a
 fatal error interrupted the request reset. The session upload progress
 handler, which runs during request startup before RINIT, then used the
 dangling pointers (use-after-free).
 .
 Targeted backport of the session/startup-state parts of php-src commit
 506e87fa7dcdd306975e5b8f8265ee03527aacbf for PHP 8.4.5: reset the session,
 serialize, URL rewriter, error handler, error list, object store and
 http_globals state before request data is processed; initialise the
 session globals at MULTIPART_EVENT_START; ignore request_parse_body();
 run the upload progress (un)serialization in an "incomplete classes only"
 mode so no user code (autoload, __wakeup, __unserialize, ...) runs before
 RINIT; and drop the temporary $_SESSION afterwards. The fallible
 allocator / delayed OOM infrastructure of the upstream commit
 (CVE-2026-109618) is intentionally not backported.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/506e87fa7dcdd306975e5b8f8265ee03527aacbf
